@meta
id: 17-15
title: A mark that remembers the file
chapter: 17
type: lesson
skills: marks-set, marks-jump
par: 145
minutes: 8
vscode: three tabs and Ctrl+Tab, then find the line again
open: order.provider.ts order.entity.ts order.repository.ts
vimrc: set hidden

@brief
Orders need a `placedAt` timestamp, which means three files.

Start in the provider. In `create`, the values passed to
`orderRepository.create` need `placedAt: new Date(), ` inserted just
before `status: 'PENDING'`. Search for `status: 'PENDING` and you are
on the `s` where it goes. Do not type it yet. Mark the spot in a way
that will still work after you have been to two other files.

Then: the entity gets `placedAt: Date;` under `total`, and the
repository's `toEntity` gets `placedAt: record.placedAt,` under its
`total` line. Two buffer switches, two searches, two inserts.

Then jump to the mark. It should take you back into the provider, to
the exact character, in one command. Finish the insert there. All
three files are graded.

@keys
| `mA` | set the global mark `A`: position and file |
| `` `A `` | jump to it, switching buffers if needed |
| `:b entity` | switch to the buffer whose name contains `entity` |
| `:marks` | list marks, including the file each uppercase one is in |
| `:wqa` | write everything, quit |

@hints
A lowercase mark is local to its file. Set `ma` in the provider and
`` `a `` from the entity means the entity's own `a`, which is unset.
--
Uppercase marks are global: one `A` for the whole session, and it
remembers which file it was set in. `` `A `` from anywhere goes there.
--
`/status: 'PENDING` Enter, `mA`. `:b entity`, `/total`,
`oplacedAt: Date;` Esc. `:b repo`, `/total`,
`oplacedAt: record.placedAt,` Esc. `` `A ``, `iplacedAt: new Date(), `
Esc, `:wqa`.

@solution
    /status: 'PENDING<Enter> mA
    :b entity<Enter> /total<Enter> oplacedAt: Date;<Esc>
    :b repo<Enter> /total<Enter> oplacedAt: record.placedAt,<Esc>
    `A iplacedAt: new Date(), <Esc> :wqa<Enter>

Twenty-six lowercase marks per file, twenty-six uppercase marks per
session. The uppercase ones carry a file name with them, and jumping
to one opens that file if it is not already showing. That is the
whole difference, and it is exactly the difference you need for "I am
about to go and touch two other files, and then I want to be back
here".

`Ctrl-O` would have worked, with four presses, if you counted the two
searches. `:b provider` would have worked, followed by a search to
find the line again. The mark was one command and no thinking, which
is the standard you should hold navigation to.

Uppercase marks are also saved between sessions, so `` `A `` tomorrow
morning still goes to the provider line, even after you have closed
vim. People keep `A` on whatever they are working on this week and
`B` on its test. The catch is the same as the benefit: there is only
one `A`, and setting it in another project overwrites it. `:marks`
shows where every mark currently points, with the file name for the
uppercase ones, when you are not sure.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    await this.customerProvider.findOne(customerId);

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    await this.customerProvider.findOne(customerId);

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, placedAt: new Date(), status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  cancellationReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@expected order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  placedAt: Date;
  cancellationReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@start order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public async findByCustomer(args: { customerId: string }) {
    const records = await this.prisma.order.findMany({
      where: { customerId: args.customerId, deleted: null },
    });

    return records.map((record) => this.toEntity(record));
  }

  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      status: record.status,
      total: record.total,
      cancellationReason: record.cancellationReason ?? undefined,
    };
  }
}

@expected order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public async findByCustomer(args: { customerId: string }) {
    const records = await this.prisma.order.findMany({
      where: { customerId: args.customerId, deleted: null },
    });

    return records.map((record) => this.toEntity(record));
  }

  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      status: record.status,
      total: record.total,
      placedAt: record.placedAt,
      cancellationReason: record.cancellationReason ?? undefined,
    };
  }
}
